# ========================================
# ADDITIONAL NOTES
# ========================================

# MIGRATION NOTES:
# 1. Hyprland's animations have no direct Sway equivalent - Sway focuses on performance
# 2. Hyprland's blur effects are not available in Sway
# 3. Some window rules may behave differently between the two compositors
# 4. hypridle/hyprlock should be replaced with swayidle/swaylock
# 5. hyprshot should be replaced with grim + slurp for screenshots
# 6. Some Hyprland-specific commands (hyprctl) need Sway equivalents (swaymsg)
# 7. You may want to install additional tools:
#    - waybar (status bar)
#    - autotiling (for automatic tiling)
#    - swaylock-effects (enhanced lock screen)
#    - swayidle (idle management)
#    - grim + slurp (screenshots)

# RECOMMENDED ADDITIONAL PACKAGES:
# - waybar: Modern status bar
# - swaylock-effects: Enhanced lock screen with effects
# - autotiling: Automatic tiling script for i3-like behavior
# - wlogout: Logout menu
# - mako or swaync: Notification daemon (you're already using swaync)

include /etc/sway/config.d/*
